  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v1.4.2 - Documentation only. Corrects v1.4.1.\n\nNo functional change. Not one selector, setter or resource key differs from v1.4.0; the assembly differs only by its embedded version stamp.\n\nThe sidebar navigation guide added in v1.4.1 was written from the working sandbox but never compiled, and it did not work as printed. Every snippet in it has now been built and run in a fresh app against this package. Three corrections:\n\n- NavPage.IsSelected is now an ObservableObject property. As printed it was a plain auto-property, which compiles and runs and leaves the navigation highlight stuck on the first page while the content area changes underneath it - no exception, no binding error.\n- The nav button's icon comes from Tag and its label from Content, which the guide now says outright. The previous snippet put an icon-and-label panel in Content, which the control template does not expect.\n- The 13 icon geometries the package ships are documented for the first time, with their keys. The old snippet referenced an icon key that does not exist; a missing key renders nothing rather than failing loudly, so it was invisible.\n\nIf you copied the v1.4.1 navigation guide into your app, the first item above is the one to check.",
